## 2. Full contract inputs (audit-only; not read by default; add --full when needed)
- 11 items; read the lean/on-demand lists above by default.

## 3. Contract outputs
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design.md (unified design: five sections for design decisions, interfaces, frontend, backend, and tests)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/figma-layout.csv (07 fills route/dom_selector in every row and defines responsive rules accordingly; geometry/text/font values follow the target-framework design code and metadata)<br>the ### PAGE→BLOCK→component mapping in openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design.md (based on the figma-code target-framework design code, registering only business adaptations and UI-DEVIATION; do not redesign styles/layout/copy)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/baseline-impact.md (07 updates the design review conclusion: NO_IMPACT/REBASE_REQUIRED and design evidence)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/baseline-binding.json (07 writes design evidence for each constraint)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/test-cases.csv (test case matrix mapping TEST ID → AC/PAGE/API/IO, including failure injection/test-double environment/manual reason; BLOCK is optional, write N/A when not applicable)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/api/openapi.yaml (applicable conditionally: when there is an API)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/api-io-mapping.csv (applicable conditionally: when there is an API)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/io-catalog.csv (applicable conditionally: when there is an API)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/design/interface-catalog.csv (cross-boundary interface catalog: HTTP/native bridge/device/third-party/async/file; applicable conditionally: when there are cross-boundary interfaces)
- openspec/changes/workflow-context-bundles/traceability.csv (merges API and test mappings; the sole traceability aggregate file)

## 4. Gates
scripts/check-change.sh <change-id>; scripts/check-design-assets.sh <change-id> --strict --lint-api (also validates figma-audit when UI is involved); scripts/check-design-sections.py --change <change-id> (including ### existing code change impact, figma-layout.csv route/dom_selector completion, and responsive rules); scripts/check-test-cases.py --change <change-id> --strict; scripts/check-traceability.py --file openspec/changes/<change-id>/traceability.csv --strict; when there is an API: scripts/check-api-traceability.py --change <change-id>; when there are cross-boundary interfaces: scripts/check-interface-catalog.py --change <change-id> --strict; python scripts/check-method-evidence.py --step 07-detailed-design --evidence <evidence> (must cover existing functionality/new functionality/code location/third-party interfaces); python3 scripts/baseline-governance.py check-change --change-id <id> --phase design

## 5. Approval and next-stage inputs
- Approval: technical lead confirms design scope, interfaces, and test approach
- unified design decisions, interface contracts, frontend/backend implementation constraints, test case matrix, figma-layout.csv assertion mapping, and the sole traceability matrix
